From: Onigiri
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the inner screen in landscape while it mirrors

onigiri-mirror fits the default display to the monitor's shape. On the
landscape cover that is fine, but the inner panel is portrait: forced to a
landscape size at rotation 0, the window manager took the panel for a
landscape one and squeezed the mirror into a strip across the middle, and
SystemUI laid out for the wrong shape and got cut off. onigiri-mirror now
gives a portrait panel the monitor's shape turned upright and sets
sys.onigiri.mirror_fit; while it is set, the default display on a portrait
panel reports a landscape orientation, so it turns to landscape whatever
apps or the lock screen ask for, and portrait-only apps are letterboxed.

diff --git a/smali_classes2/com/android/server/wm/DisplayContent.smali b/smali_classes2/com/android/server/wm/DisplayContent.smali
--- a/smali_classes2/com/android/server/wm/DisplayContent.smali
+++ b/smali_classes2/com/android/server/wm/DisplayContent.smali
@@ -12531,6 +12531,31 @@
     return v3
 
     :cond_1
+    # Onigiri: while onigiri-mirror fits the default display to a monitor, it sets
+    # sys.onigiri.mirror_fit and gives a portrait panel (the inner screen) the monitor's shape
+    # turned upright. Keep that panel in landscape, whatever apps or the lock screen ask for, so
+    # it shows the mirror the way the monitor does. The landscape cover keeps its own rotation.
+    iget v1, v0, Lcom/android/server/wm/DisplayContent;->mDisplayId:I
+
+    if-nez v1, :onigiri_mirror_fit_done
+
+    iget v1, v0, Lcom/android/server/wm/DisplayContent;->mInitialDisplayWidth:I
+
+    iget v4, v0, Lcom/android/server/wm/DisplayContent;->mInitialDisplayHeight:I
+
+    if-ge v1, v4, :onigiri_mirror_fit_done
+
+    const-string v1, "sys.onigiri.mirror_fit"
+
+    invoke-static {v1, v2}, Landroid/os/SystemProperties;->getBoolean(Ljava/lang/String;Z)Z
+
+    move-result v1
+
+    if-eqz v1, :onigiri_mirror_fit_done
+
+    return v2
+
+    :onigiri_mirror_fit_done
     iget-boolean v1, v0, Lcom/android/server/wm/DisplayContent;->isDefaultDisplay:Z
 
     const/4 v4, -0x2
